# Rule: Client arcs (/arcs)

Mirror of [`.claude/rules/arcs.md`](../../.claude/rules/arcs.md) — read
that file; it is the canonical text. Read first: ADR-052 (the deck
chassis), ADR-057 (terminal motion), ADR-072 (the portfolio arc, the
`dossier` section kind, the shared evidence, the envelope on arcs), ADR-073
(the site's header on every arc; the left reel deleted), ADR-090 (the
dossier is one housing — proposed), ADR-098 (clients, the overview's
filter, the `configuration` kind, the scaffold — proposed).

⚠ ADR-098: an `ArcDef` gains `client` / `kind` / `theme`, and `/arcs/<client>`
lists that client's engagements INSIDE the existing `[slug]` route — the two
slug sets share a namespace and are pinned disjoint. NO URL MOVED: engagements
stay flat, because an arc's whole distribution is a link somebody forwarded.
`kind` is DERIVED from `format` where it can be, so no pre-existing content
module was edited; `format` stays the LAYOUT family (a portfolio and a
proposal are both productions and lay out alike). The overview groups by
client and filters by kind, writing ONE attribute with the narrowing in CSS
over server-rendered `data-kind` / `data-kinds` — no `:has()`, and no
attribute means everything is shown. The `configuration` kind is ADR-052's
SECOND exception to "content-only" after the dossier: one client leaf, one
delegated listener, the resting state authored, `data-cfg-*` never
`data-arc-*`, and the pitch page's grammar COPIED onto the ADR-077 ramp
rather than shared. A `theme: "light"` arc is two halves — the mount and a
hand-written `LIGHT_LOCKED_ROUTES` row. `scripts/new-arc.mjs` scaffolds a
client page in one command and ships finished copy, never placeholders.

⚠ ADR-098 U1: the journey row in the top-left corner is hidden on EVERY
surface now — the arcs asked, then the homepage, so the rule and the bracket's
return live in `rail-instruments.css` (the ≤960 rung promoted to every width)
and the route-scoped copies in `arcs.css` and `trinny-london.css` are deleted.
Do not re-add one. `display: none`, never unmounted, so the rosters stay
exercised. Unlike the pitch page an arc KEEPS its section indicator: the
header is the site's own. And a
PROPOSAL's interstitial line drops to `clamp(24px, 2.6vw, 40px)` at 42ch,
scoped to the format — a deck is presented in a room, a proposal is read at
arm's length.

⚠ ADR-090: the four dossier beats are one machined housing (ADR-089's
grammar at page scale) with the console as a square CELL inside it, all
`.arc-dossier`-scoped and gated at `(min-width: 981px) and
(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`. Three traps, all measured: the
ADR-052 reveal's `rootMargin: -10%` is a DEAD BAND the housing may not fill
into (`--dos-reveal-clear`; the cost is double the clearance, and it binds
only at tall viewports where the console sets the row); `.arc-head` carries
`.arc-reveal`, whose transform is the containing block, so the header
band's seat is declared rather than inherited; and the housing's inset is
paid for by the FIELD, where `.fl-bay__top` is already clipped. The housing
also makes `--arc-plate` the record column's BED in light — a new text rung
there belongs in the contrast walk.

⚠ ADR-100: the `board` kind is the FOURTH enumerated exception — the client's
configuration as a circuit board in two states (dormant beside lit), the
proof's R4 grammar at page scale, no frame, one leaf with no picker, SERVER-ONLY.
⚠ U1 (owner, same day: "no, radically simplify it") is the live cut — FOUR
objects per board (seat · layer · card · tools), one line apiece, three plain
ribbons; the bed, sockets, foot rows, hatch, layer sentences, second card row
and the elastic crop (`ArcBoardRow`) are deleted. When he asks for simple, the
FIRST cut is the minimal one. Dispatched in BOTH `ArcSectionRenderer` and the
Trinny page's `TrinnyBeats` switch (which dropped `configuration`;
`ArcConfiguration` is byte-identical elsewhere). The row is width-led and its
shares are the crops' (560 + 40 + 800 = 1400; the flex bases and the seam are
pinned by `arc-board-fit`; the svg sits at its own height, no cap, no aspect);
every colour is an `--arc-board-*` alias of the ramp, never a `--pda-*`; every
dormant rule sits under `.is-arc-js` + `no-preference` so no-JS and PRM render
lit; `data-board-*` never `data-arc-*`; the head on the TEXT band, the drawing
on the INSTRUMENT band.

Contracts in one breath: one scroll writer (`useArcScroll`); `--hero-lift`
gates the rails; the slice API is read-only; every section opaque void; no
three.js / Supabase / `LandingPage` imports — the casefile's dossier LEAVES
(`ToolField`, `MediaLightbox`, `ConsoleFrame`, `wireframes/**`,
`toolCardData`) are the one sanctioned import; page CSS lives in `arcs.css`
under `.arc-*`, with the casefile's `casefile.css` + `console.css` imported
at the ROUTE ahead of it and `theme.css` last; no italics; content changes
= `lib/arcs/content/*` + the registry; shared Loop evidence is imported by
reference from `content/shared/*`; the numbers canon fails on every arc;
the confidentiality envelope runs over the portfolio (the keynote deck
keeps its € rows — recorded); a dossier beat must FIT at 1280×720 /
1440×800 / 1920×1080; a bay change is a two-surface change (run the ring
smoke AND the portfolio smoke); the header is `ArcHudNav` (the landing's
`.hud__nav*` chrome — chapter links in the hero, the readout + drawer once
scrolled) and `ArcMenu` is deleted, with `menuPrimary` marking a chapter.
